<title>GERMANY: German July trade surplus rises to 10.9 bln DM.</title>
<headline>German July trade surplus rises to 10.9 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC July 96   June 96	 July 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		+10.9     +7.0	    +6.0</p>
<p> Current account	    - 4.4     -2.1	    -5.4</p>
<p> Exports			 67.5     60.9	    58.0</p>
<p> Imports			 56.6     53.9	    52.0</p>
<p> Services			-6.7     -4.3	    -5.4</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -3.7     +0.9	    -0.7</p>
<p> Transfers		     -4.7     -5.3	    -4.9</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 -0.2     -0.4	    -0.4</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Jan-July 96	Jan-July 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		   56.5		50.5</p>
<p> Current account		-13.1		-9.5</p>
<p> Exports			  438.6	     420.8</p>
<p> Imports			  382.1	     370.3</p>
<p> Services			 -30.9	     -31.5</p>
<p> Wage and property income    -5.2		+3.6</p>
<p> Transfers			-31.6	     -30.4</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -1.9		-1.7</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
